# Today's scripts, scenes and data the rebuilt client runs, copied from godot/ at the same paths by tools/rebuild/sync-code.mjs (DECISIONS B43).
# One glob per line, relative to godot/; `!glob` leaves files out. `*` stays inside a folder, `**` crosses folders, a folder name takes it whole.
# Code files only (scripts and their uids, scenes, resources, shaders, data); assets go through client/assets.list. Never edit a copy in
# client/: change godot/ and sync, or port the file (--port). Left out on purpose: the per-creature systems the combat core replaces.

# ==== Copied: the game's code, scenes and data (whole folders; the leave-outs below take their parts out again)
audio      # AudioDirector (autoload), mixer, music, ambience, sample bank, the audio map
data       # content, combat, loot, progression and world JSON the rules and the core read
front      # login, character select, the front flow
fx         # Vfx (autoload), the Binbun controllers, primitives, the gallery
game       # avatar and creature rigs, boss telegraphs, event fx, inventory, loadout, settings, gathering and labor views
game_ui    # the panel host, tooltips, chat commands, tips, mock game
loot_view  # the loot drop view
main       # boot, audio hooks, camera rig, crash watch, assets pack loader, perf overlay
net        # API client, config, kill reporter, update check, mock backend
next       # the game scene folder: its non-seam parts (HUD parts, area milestones, depths, hub NPCs, rewards, world)
rules      # combat, loot, gear, progression, gathering and inventory rules
session    # DmSession and its bodies
sim        # pure sim helpers: nav, depths floors and rules, boss brains, exact math, shared constants
ui         # theme, HUD kit, panels, widgets, onboarding
world      # world builder, model loader, occlusion shaders, animator
world_fx   # world dressing and atmosphere

# ==== Ported (client/code.lock.json "ported"; edited in client/, so the sync leaves them alone and reports one whose original changed)
# next/next_game.gd, next/next_game.tscn   the game scene on DmCoreHost: a solo run in the Graves with a test-server character or a dev one, with the Gravecaller's rites and the Gravedigger King; refuses any api but the test server's; the warm-up on request (opts.warmup); host or guest of a 2-player party (a puppet core on the guest), the friends list, online for friends' presence; value on the server on the host (rewards, meta, Chronicle, progression, the loot node); no gathering, Chapterhouse, Codex, full HUD
# next/next_world.gd                       loads client/areas/<id>.tscn and its navigation map instead of the runtime DmWorldBuilder build; the same small API
# next/next_input.gd                       the hover pick asks the core; the chase and the queued casts are today's (DmCombatInput); Easy auto combat is back (`auto`, closed until the settings or a gate_probe open it)
# next/spawn/dm_wave_director.gd           spawns through the core (ids); counts from the core; no Grave Surges, no clearing of living bodies
# next/hero/dm_hero_body.gd                an external of the core; enemy blows arrive by id (EV_TARGET_HIT); no collider; thralls counted by the core
# next/hero/dm_hero_look.gd                the hovered-enemy ring reads the core by id
# next/enemy_fx/dm_enemy_fx.gd             an event consumer: the core's telegraphs, strikes, deaths, zones and affix moments (no node per enemy)
# game/dm_avatar.gd                        its own three motion helpers instead of DmEntityViews'
# game/dm_event_fx.gd, game/dm_event_fx_zones.gd   zone and corpse records read by field name (no DmSimZone, DmSimCorpse)
# main/main.gd, main/main.tscn             the boot (DmMain): the front flow against the TEST server, then the game scene with the chosen character, its bag and progression (DmMain.load_build); `--benchmark` and the Benchmark button (the run is sent to the test server only); the party hand-over (join_ready, client_ended, a failed join); no crash report, Log out or Switch character
# net/dm_config.gd                         the TEST server's, lobby's and relay's addresses and the allow-list (DmConfig.allows_url, allows_api_base, allows_lobby_url, allows_relay); the live ones never appear (tests/front.gd)
# net/dm_http_transport.gd                 refuses any request DmConfig does not allow
# Easy auto combat and the benchmark (client/README.md "The benchmark"):
# next/feel/dm_next_auto.gd                the adapter reads the core: the bulk arrays (enemy_ids / positions / states, corpse_ids / positions) and the facts the host's signals keep (radius, elite, health, wind-up, corpse kind, hostile zones); same decisions, same intents
# next/perf/dm_benchmark.gd                the Hollow Graves and the Gravecaller only (refused otherwise); the core's step, crowd sync and event dispatch per tick timed (DmCoreHost.measure) for the report's budget section; the HUD's share
# next/perf/dm_bench_fight.gd              boots the game scene; the counts are held through the core (top_up through the director, trim by remove_enemy, thralls raised into the core)
# next/perf/dm_benchmark_screen.gd, next/perf/dm_benchmark_setup.gd   the budget section on the results; the rooms and classes the client has; the upload note names the test server; a headless run quits by itself
# next/perf/dm_next_warmup.gd, game/dm_warmup.gd   the boss models, effects and gear drawn once, every crowd model from rehearsal rows, the area tour; no per-creature bodies (DmWarmup's old own warm-up is gone); on request only
# Graphics presets (client/README.md "Graphics presets", DECISIONS B45):
# game/dm_graphics_preset.gd               today's four presets on Forward+: no prop-light count or prop shadow range (baked), ambient occlusion, the crowd's shadow policy, apply_environment
# next/perf/dm_next_perf.gd                applies a preset to the game scene: moon, environment, viewport, the crowd's shadow policy, fx; Auto resolution upscales with FSR 1; no caster poll
# Copied again because of them: next/perf/dm_bench_history.gd.
# 2-player co-op (client/README.md "Co-op on the core"):
# next/next_net.gd                         the core's snapshot (cut by body ranges to fit a packet), reliable batches and baseline over the session's peer, the heroes' ids and vitals, a guest's request for a baseline; no enemy dictionaries or cues (the core's events carry them)
# next/party/dm_next_party.gd              the lobby link, hosting, joining, invites and asks against the TEST lobby and relay (DmConfig), friendship changes announced (friends_changed), the host's world (heat, difficulty) told to the lobby, the host <-> guest handshake of the guest's own account (B22); no chat or ground drops
# session/dm_session.gd                    the hello carries the core's wire version (DmCore.wire_version(), PROTOCOL 3) and the host refuses another; `abort(reason)` for a guest the host's messages cannot be used by
# The Gravedigger King (client/README.md "The Gravedigger King"): the boss is an external of the core (kind 1) whose brain stays GDScript; the brains of sim/bosses are copies, unchanged:
# next/bosses/dm_boss.gd                   a plain node (no DmEnemy, no collider, no agent, no state machine) that registers as an external of the core (core_id) and takes blows through take_damage
# next/bosses/dm_boss_host.gd              summon rules and events as today; the thralls' blows come from the core (thrall_hit_external); the Gravedigger's area only (served_areas); no pools
# next/bosses/dm_boss_node_world.gd        the brain's world on the core: adds through the director's spawn, remove_enemy, the core's thralls and corpses; no pools, no set_enemy_hp
# next/bosses/dm_boss_fx.gd                no pool_visual (the Saint's rot, with the Saint)
# game/dm_boss_view.gd                     its own three motion helpers instead of DmEntityViews'
# Copied again because of them: next/bosses/dm_boss_meta.gd (the Covenant Seal altar choice; it needs the panels' prompt, so nothing creates it yet).
# Copied again because of them: next/status (DmStatusSet, for the status sets of heroes and bosses only), next/enemy_fx/dm_enemy_fx_host.gd, game/dm_event_fx_telegraph.gd,
# game/dm_event_fx_boss.gd, next/progress/dm_next_chronicle.gd, next/areas/dm_area_flow.gd, next/gathering/dm_next_gather.gd.
# The HUD on the core (client/README.md "The HUD on the core"; its draw-call budget: "The HUD's budget"):
# next/next_hud.gd                         the HUD host (DmNextHud): today's DmHud fed by the view-model on a 20 Hz timer from the core's signals; floating numbers with the caps; banners; hud_scale and hud_layout options; the menu row shows the Social button only and brings the Social window (next/hud/dm_next_social.gd)
# next/hud/dm_next_hud_vm.gd               the view-model from the core's bulk arrays (target frame, minimap dots, thrall count, corpses near the hero, cooldowns); no DmThrallHost, DmEnemy or DmCorpseField
# game/dm_game_hud.gd                      only the art path and the interaction prompts: the old game's view-model builder (DmSimEnemy) is gone
# ui/hud/dm_hud.gd                         the pieces (movable, scalable: set_piece, set_layout, show_piece), drawn from one atlas on z layers, floats from a pool
# ui/hud/dm_hud_kit.gd                     the layers (Z_PANEL .. Z_FLOATS), plate / rect / outline / gradient_rect from the atlas, the draw-call model's log; `style` still gives a StyleBoxFlat (copied panels ask for it)
# ui/hud/dm_hud_bar.gd, dm_hud_parts.gd, dm_hud_orb.gd, dm_hud_slot.gd, dm_hud_minimap.gd, dm_hud_brew_chip.gd   rectangles from the atlas, vector art as one mesh per widget, the dots as a MultiMesh
# ui/widgets/dm_toast.gd, dm_banner.gd, dm_corners.gd   a 9-patch panel and atlas rectangles
# Client-only files beside them (not copies): next/hud/dm_hud_atlas.gd (the runtime atlas), dm_hud_mesh.gd (triangle bags), dm_hud_floats.gd (the pool of floating numbers).
# The Gravecaller's rites on the core (client/README.md "The Gravecaller's rites"): enemies are ids and DmFoe snapshots, a blow is `c.deal`, a status `c.apply_status`, the corpse field
# is core/dm_core_corpses.gd and the legion core/dm_core_legion.gd (the core's own, not copies):
# next/rites/dm_rite_caster.gd, dm_rite_module.gd, dm_rite_legends.gd, dm_rite_registry.gd   the plumbing; the registry lists the necromancer's 25 (the Reaper's nine wait for the Reaper)
# next/rites/rite_*.gd  (24 of the 25; rite_veil_step.gd needed no change and is a copy)   black_litany, bone_fan, bone_mantle, bone_needle, bone_prison, bone_storm, carrion_seed, command_rend,
#                                          corpse_explosion, dirge, exhume, grave_frost, grave_hands, grave_offering, grave_step, ivory_cleave, marrow_spear, miasma, ossuary_wall (the wall is not solid
#                                          for the core's enemies yet), plague_bloom, rally_dead, rot_lance, soul_siphon, wailing_skull
# game/dm_rite_fx.gd                       the Reaper's green is a constant of its own (the one thing it took from DmReaperRites)
# next/feel/dm_combat_input.gd             the attack target is the core's enemy id; the caster says whether it is alive and hittable
# Copied again because of them: next/rites/dm_rite_hotbar.gd, next/rites/rite_veil_step.gd, next/progress/dm_next_belt.gd.
# Value on the server (client/README.md "Value on the server"): kills are the game's `kill_credited`, the bag is the game's `loot` (client-only next/rewards/dm_next_loot.gd:
# today's DmNextUiHost take, pickup, claim and rune-ownership paths on their own):
# next/rewards/dm_session_rewards.gd       kills from `kill_credited` (the killer is a peer), lifesteal from DmCoreHost.struck; no watch_enemy / attach_spawner
# next/meta/dm_next_meta.gd                a kill's enemy is a core id; the Bonded Dead rise through the hero's legion on the core (DmCoreLegion.raise_bonded)
# next/progress/dm_next_progress.gd        the bag is the loot node's (the server's rows until it exists)
# next/areas/dm_wave_milestones.gd         the Nightfall light dims the world's lights (DmNextWorld.builder); banners through the game's `game_event`
# next/party/dm_next_joiner.gd             a party guest's own account; its bag is the loot node's
# The effects (client/README.md "The benchmark"; native/README.md "Files"):
# fx/dm_fx_ring.gd                         the motes and the per-frame loop are the core's DmMotes (C++); the random start of each mote is still made here (client/tests/fx_motes.gd)

# ==== Per-creature systems the combat core and the crowd view replace: not copied (DECISIONS B42, B43)
!enemies                      # DmEnemy, its states, kinds and scenes: the core owns enemies
!sim/sim_enemy.gd             # DmSimEnemy record
!sim/sim_thrall.gd            # DmSimThrall record
!sim/sim_corpse.gd            # DmSimCorpse record
!sim/sim_zone.gd              # DmSimZone record
!next/thralls                 # DmThrall, DmThrallHost and the thrall scenes
!next/corpses                 # DmCorpseField
!next/affixes                 # DmAffixSet
!game/dm_entity_views.gd      # DmEntityViews: per-creature nodes, replaced by the crowd view

# ==== Seams: ported to the core in later steps (each uses a per-creature class or scene)
!game/dm_caster_budget.gd                 # uses DmEnemy, DmEnemyState
!main/qa_driver.gd                        # uses DmEnemy
!next/areas/dm_grave_surge.gd             # uses DmEnemy
!next/chapterhouse/dm_chapterhouse.gd     # uses DmThrallHost
!next/depths/dm_depths.gd                 # uses DmEnemy, DmEnemyState, DmThrallHost
!next/hud/dm_next_counsel.gd              # uses DmEnemy, DmEnemyState, DmThrallHost
!next/hud/dm_next_ui_host.gd              # uses DmSimCorpse, DmEnemy, DmEnemyState +3: the host-contract adapter of the panels (DmGameUi); the HUD runs without it, the panels bring it back
!next/progress/dm_next_codex.gd           # uses DmEnemy
!next/rites/dm_reaper_rites.gd            # uses DmEnemy, DmStatusSet
!next/rites/rite_scythe_weave.gd          # uses DmEnemy
!next/rites/rite_unleash_souls.gd         # uses DmEnemy, DmStatusSet
!next/rites/rite_wraith_walk.gd           # uses DmEnemy, DmStatusSet

